a blockage in the fuel pipe.","q":true,"src":"goldenera.fi","c":9},{"lap":1,"text":"But in corrected time, Boyer, who made the same time as DePalma, was leading ahead of DePalma and Murphy","q":true,"src":"goldenera.fi","c":10},{"lap":2,"text":"Murphy leads on corrected time after a 7m58s lap.","q":false,"c":0},{"lap":5,"text":"After 5 laps, 86.310 km, Murphy had raised his advantage to half a minute over Boyer.","q":true,"src":"goldenera.fi","c":0},{"lap":7,"text":"Murphy laps in 7m43s at 132.2 km/h as DePalma, Chassagne and Murphy pass the grandstand nose to tail.","q":false,"c":0},{"lap":7,"text":"Mathis retired with engine trouble on the seventh lap after having completing only five laps.","q":true,"src":"goldenera.fi","c":12},{"lap":8,"text":"On the eighth lap Andr\u00e9 Boillot received great applause when he changed his rear tire in the unbelievable time of 35 seconds.","q":true,"src":"goldenera.fi","c":4},{"lap":10,"text":"After 10 laps, 172.620 km, Murphy had raised his advantage to over 1 minute to Chassagne and Boyer.","q":true,"src":"goldenera.fi","c":0},{"lap":12,"text":"Murphy stops two minutes for fuel and rear tyres; Chassagne and Boyer get past.","q":false,"c":0},{"lap":12,"text":"The excitement grew as Chassagne's blue Ballot took over the lead under thundering applause of the French crowd, with an advantage of 1m10s at the end of lap 12.","q":true,"src":"goldenera.fi","c":11},{"lap":12,"text":"De Palma stopped at the pits on the 12th lap for over four minutes.","q":true,"src":"goldenera.fi","c":1},{"lap":15,"text":"After 15 laps, 258.930 km, Chassagne in the leading Ballot was half a minute ahead of Boyer's Duesenberg and maintained his advantage of over 1 minute to Murphy.","q":true,"src":"goldenera.fi","c":11},{"lap":17,"text":"Boyer retires at La Tertre with a broken connecting rod; a stone had punctured his radiator.","q":false,"c":10},{"lap":18,"text":"Chassagne pits from the lead: the fuel tank mounts have fractured and the split tank is beyond pit repair.","q":false,"c":11},{"lap":18,"text":"With the field now down to ten cars, the lead went back to Murphy.","q":true,"src":"goldenera.fi","c":0},{"lap":19,"text":"De Palma made his second pit stop on the 19th lap for over four minutes.","q":true,"src":"goldenera.fi","c":1},{"lap":20,"text":"After 20 laps, 345.240 km, Murphy had a lead of 1m21s over Guyot's Duesenberg.","q":true,"src":"goldenera.fi","c":0},{"lap":26,"text":"DePalma pits a third time; the seam of his fuel tank has opened.","q":false,"c":1},{"lap":28,"text":"Guyot stops for tyres, fuel and water; his exhausted mechanic is replaced by spectator Arthur Duray.","q":false,"c":5},{"lap":29,"text":"Thomas, many laps down, retires when a flying stone holes the oil tank.","q":false,"c":9},{"lap":29,"text":"Guyot stops again with a slipping clutch; DePalma moves up to second.","q":false,"c":5},{"lap":30,"text":"Murphy slowed down on his last lap to 10m31s due to a slow puncture in a rear tire.","q":true,"src":"goldenera.fi","c":0},{"lap":30,"text":"Murphy waved happily to de Knyff as he crossed the finish line, with his ribs taped, his radiator was empty for the last ten minutes of the race, a stone having hole it and his right rear tire was flat.","q":true,"src":"goldenera.fi","c":0},{"lap":30,"text":"Jimmy Murphy had finished after 4h07m11.4s at an average of more than 125 km/h.","q":true,"src":"goldenera.fi","c":0}]}